  "transcript": [
    {
      "s": 5.07,
      "e": 12.07,
      "text": "Honestly, I was really pumped up that we got a chance to use our training to actually help people out."
    },
    {
      "s": 12.07,
      "e": 21.07,
      "text": "We go to AT every year, drill after drill, we train on backhose and bobcats and dump trucks."
    },
    {
      "s": 21.07,
      "e": 28.07,
      "text": "I'm just glad that we got a chance to finally use our equipment and use our training to help out some people that really need it."
    },
    {
      "s": 29.07,
      "e": 34.07,
      "text": "Just devastation really, like the entire town just wiped out."
    },
    {
      "s": 34.07,
      "e": 36.07,
      "text": "You wouldn't even be able to recognize it."
    },
    {
      "s": 36.07,
      "e": 40.07,
      "text": "We were talking about it just a little bit ago, wondering what the town looked like beforehand."
    },
    {
      "s": 40.07,
      "e": 45.07,
      "text": "Because all you see is debris, trees blown over, houses and pieces."
    },
    {
      "s": 45.07,
      "e": 51.07,
      "text": "People picking up their belongings. I mean, it's just absolutely, it's just horrible."
    }
  ],
